\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces AskWearables{} raised accuracy for the models that were weak with raw context; no model was significantly less accurate with it. Accuracy in \% with Wilson 95\% intervals; $p$ is the exact McNemar test on paired tasks, with the number of tasks only \textsf  {C}{} answered correctly and only the other condition answered correctly in parentheses. Superscript $n$ marks cells with fewer than 100{} scored runs. 5{} of the 5{} significant differences against \textsf  {A}{}, and 4{} of the 4{} against \textsf  {B}{}, remain significant after Holm correction over all 18{} tests.}}{16}{table.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
